/-!
# One-level channel calibration + production audit

Gates the anti-circular calibration / identifiability / held-out-prediction surface of the one-level
LDDL channel, its strict entropy-production content, and the quantum H-theorem it inherits: the rate
calibration and its injectivity, the held-out occupation prediction's anchors and its dependence on only
the identified parameters, the binary relative-entropy floor and explicit form, the strict positivity of
the production rate away from equilibrium, the monotone relaxation of the occupation deviation, the
stationary diagonal state and its channel fixed-point property, the antitone entropic proper time along
the discrete channel orbit (from data-processing), the one-step clock contraction, and the vanishing of
discrete Spohn production at equilibrium. All are exact identities / inequalities (kernel-clean,
non-definitional).
-/

